const requiredObservations=[
  {id:'catalog_authoritative_sources',requirement:'Review real table ownership, canonical DDL, installation/key/version, original owner/write deadline provenance, row/evidence binding, artifact state, holds, leases and all incoming uses. Supply positive expired terminal and contradictory/active/foreign-source controls. No made-up SQL columns or inherited child deadline.'},
  {id:'complete_program_visibility',requirement:'In an owned disposable fixture, independently seed a trigger, procedure, function, event and view. A privileged observer must enumerate exact identities and complete non-NULL definitions, parameters/return types and compile/security context. Prove that the worker or a restricted observer can omit rows/bodies; absence without independently verified visibility must remain not_ready.'},
  {id:'program_change_after_capture',requirement:'Change a trigger/routine/event after the initial capture. Prove the approved freeze blocks the change through the collector commit, or prove the full policy rejects and rolls back all group/tombstone/capacity writes. Two matching samples alone do not close the final-check-to-commit race.'},
  {id:'same_schema_table_ddl',requirement:'Attempt ALTER/DROP and creation of a new reference table during the complete proposed freeze. Map exact holder/writer CONNECTION_IDs to metadata_locks; distinguish actual pending locks from permissions, syntax failures or timeouts. DDL happens only in an exact UID/server/owned test database.'},
  {id:'foreign_schema_fk_and_program',requirement:'Exercise an incoming cross-schema FK and a program with cross-schema effects using separate owned test schemas. No TABLE_SCHEMA-local filter may establish global absence. Observe real metadata locks; an ordinary RR read alone is not accepted as a complete freeze.'},
  {id:'lock_tables_transaction_boundary',requirement:'Use an isolated disposable sentinel to demonstrate the documented implicit commit before LOCK TABLES and loss of prior explicit locks after START TRANSACTION. Never issue these inside the collector. The GC account grant named LOCK TABLES is a permission prerequisite, not evidence that a freeze was acquired.'},
  {id:'observer_lifecycle_and_revocation',requirement:'Close/reconnect the observer and revoke relevant privileges on held and new sessions. The full policy must reject loss of the original observation/freeze identity and must not silently reacquire or renew its lifetime. Record release of the original exact connection.'},
  {id:'single_gc_transaction',requirement:'In an actual complete Collect fixture, inject late changes after tombstone insertion and group deletion. Verify one known commit only on success and full original rows, capacity and absent tombstone on rejection. Metadata-only capture and component tests cannot substitute for this proof.'}
];
